 ],
 "says": "A steward founds a Team (team.found) and publishes one journal-mode choice into the Team's decision source (memory.record.publish), which the person working in a repository may not read. For that person's question the steward issues a state proof (memory.state.prove): addressed to the person, over the source's committed head, disclosing only that record's id and that it is current, with no reason, body or alternatives. The person resolves the question with that proof (memory.state.resolve) and gets a qualified state whose one entry is that record, current, at that frontier; from it they store a candidate for their own repository that relies on the record by id, states only what the proof disclosed, and lists its reason as unrecorded (memory.candidate.store). Two things must not disclose more: resolving the same question with a proof the steward issued for another question leaves the entry unresolved with state_proof_out_of_scope, and reading the Team source's bodies (reader.body.read) is answered denied with access_not_established — no source, unit, count, continuation or waiting use is named, which is not the same as an empty answer. No step infers a withheld reason, names another record, or claims the person received any Team event.",
 "spec_sha256": "dc38f25c1902b5e95c16bcb559dc633011cb24961709d2bcc04921f033a630ea",
